<section id="terms" class="page"><div class="welcome"><div><div class="eyebrow">CLEAR BY DESIGN</div><h1>How Jirani works</h1><p>Plain-language terms for this prototype.</p></div></div><div class="widecard legal"><span class="pill">DEMO TERMS · 17 OCT 2026</span><h3>1. Prototype only</h3><p>Jirani is a visual and interactive prototype. It is not a live rewards service. Credits shown on screen, including the KSh 10 welcome amount and activity/referral rewards, are illustrative only. They are not money, a debt, stored value, or redeemable for cash or goods.</p><h3>2. No deposits, fees, or paid unlocks</h3><p>Joining and viewing activities in this prototype is free. Never send money to access a task or unlock a promised reward. Paid tiers at KSh 40, 50, 100, or 200 are intentionally not enabled. A real paid service would need clearly disclosed pricing, refund rules, a sustainable reward budget, and appropriate legal review before launch.</p><h3>3. Fixed activity rewards</h3><p>Eligible activities show a fixed demo amount before you begin. Finishing the activity adds that amount to this browser's simulated balance once. There are no random prize draws, betting, chance-based cash rewards, or guaranteed earnings claims. Availability in a live product would depend on published eligibility and budget limits.</p><h3>4. Referrals</h3><p>The KSh 5 referral amount is also simulated. In a live service, one referral credit could be granted only after a genuine new person signs up and completes a qualifying action, subject to clear limits and fraud checks. No chain or multi-level commissions.</p><h3>5. Payouts and M-Pesa</h3><p>No real payout can be requested here. This prototype does not connect to M-Pesa, collect payment credentials, or verify transactions. A live payout flow must use an authorized payment provider, show fees and minimums, and give a receipt and support route.</p><h3>6. Fair use</h3><p>Do not create duplicate accounts, automate tasks, or submit false referrals. A production service should explain any review or account restriction and provide a way to appeal.</p><h3>7. Contact and launch status</h3><p>This preview has no operator support channel and is not open for public enrollment. Before a real launch, publish the legal operator name, contact details, final terms, complaint process, and any required registrations.</p></div></section>
<section id="privacy" class="page"><div class="welcome"><div><div class="eyebrow">YOUR DATA, YOUR CHOICE</div><h1>Privacy notice</h1><p>What this local preview stores and what a real service must explain.</p></div></div><div class="widecard legal"><span class="pill">DEMO PRIVACY · 17 OCT 2026</span><h3>What this prototype stores</h3><p>To make this preview interactive, your browser stores a demo balance, completed activity IDs, and a small activity list in local storage on this device. This information is not sent to a server. Use “Reset demo” in the Admin preview to clear it.</p><h3>What it does not collect</h3><p>This prototype does not ask for your phone number, ID, M-Pesa PIN, financial account, precise location, or contacts. Do not enter sensitive personal information.</p><h3>Production privacy requirements</h3><p>A live service should identify its data controller, explain the lawful purpose and retention period for each data type, secure account and payout information, provide access/correction/deletion contact routes, and disclose any processors or cross-border transfers before collecting data.</p><h3>Cookies and analytics</h3><p>No analytics or advertising tracking is included in this single-file preview. Browser local storage is used only to remember demo interactions.</p></div></section>
